This figure (Fig. 1/9) demonstrates the immunopotentiating effect of Nano-11 compared to aluminum hydroxide (AH) adjuvant on antigen-specific antibody responses. It shows that both Nano-11 and AH significantly enhance IgG titers against recombinant protective antigen (rPA) in mice. Notably, Nano-11 exhibits comparable adjuvanticity to AH at high doses and maintains significant efficacy even at a low dose (12.5 µg), where AH fails to induce a robust immune response. The results indicate Nano-11's potential as an effective vaccine adjuvant for boosting humoral immunity.